---
import HomeSection from './HomeSection.astro';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { buttonVariants } from '../ui/button-variants';
import { whitepaperUrl } from '../../lib/links';

// What the oracle is built for, before the walkthrough shows how. The pattern follows the user's DIA
// reference (a claim per card: a concrete list, a one-line summary, a closing line). Claims follow the
// January 2026 whitepaper: its title (bribery-resistant), §2 (any multiple-choice question; no
// centralized backstops or vetoes; secured by economic incentives), §2.1 (almost all losing bonds go to
// winners; a fork is the backstop) and §2.2 (supply restoration; attack cost above 100% of market cap
// under the paper's assumptions, hence "designed to"). The question kinds are illustrative.
// `animation` briefs the animation planned for each card; the cards show no stage until
// one is built.
const reasons = [
  {
    title: 'Resolve any question',
    text: 'Elections, sports results, flight delays, scientific claims. One oracle for any multiple-choice question, including ones no data feed can answer.',
    animation: 'Questions of every kind arrive, and each one settles on one of its outcomes.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Question every answer',
    text: 'No committee, multisig or veto. Anyone can challenge any answer, and a challenge that holds wins almost all of the losing bonds. Secured by incentives, not authority.',
    animation: 'An answer meets a challenge; the challenge holds and collects almost all of the losing bond.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Bribery-resistant by design',
    text: 'Escalating bonds, a last-resort fork, supply restoration. Forcing a false answer is designed to cost more than the oracle’s entire market cap. Built for the day someone tries to buy the answer.',
    animation: 'Bonds escalate until the oracle forks; value follows the honest side and the attacker’s copy empties.',
  },
];
const steps = [
  { title: 'Ask', text: 'Define the question, outcomes and criteria. Pay a fee.' },
  { title: 'Report', text: 'A reporter proposes an answer and locks REP, the protocol’s token, as a bond.' },
  { title: 'Challenge', text: 'A challenger can post a different answer with a larger bond.' },
  { title: 'Finalize', text: 'An answer becomes final if no one challenges it during its appeal period.' },
];
// January 2026 whitepaper §§4.1–4.5. These amounts illustrate the paper's example, not live fees.
const scenes = [
  { label: 'Possible outcomes', answer: 'Yes / No / Invalid', note: 'The question and criteria are set before reporting.', amount: '15', cost: 'Query fee' },
  { label: 'Reported answer', answer: 'No', note: 'The reporter follows the criteria: independent replication is missing.', amount: '15', cost: 'Reporting bond' },
  { label: 'Answer under review', answer: 'No', note: 'No one challenges this report during the appeal period.', amount: '15', cost: 'Bond at stake' },
  { label: 'Final outcome', answer: 'No', note: 'The appeal period ends. The application can use this answer.', amount: '15', cost: 'Bond returned' },
];
---

<HomeSection id="protocol">
  <Fragment slot="title">Built for<br />high-stakes questions</Fragment>
  <p slot="aside">When money rides on an answer, someone will try to fake it. Augur Lituus, the next generation of Augur’s oracle, is designed to hold up anyway.</p>

  <div class="why-how" data-why-how>
    <ul class="principles" data-reveal>
      {reasons.map(reason => (
        <li>
          <h3 class="augur-type-editorial-section">{reason.title}</h3>
          <p class="web-body-small">{reason.text}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <div class="process-story">
      <hgroup class="process-heading" data-reveal>
        <p>A resolution example</p>
        <h3 class="augur-type-editorial-section">One question.<br />A path to an answer.</h3>
      </hgroup>
      <div class="process-layout" data-reveal-children>
        <div class="process-guide">
          <ol class="process-steps" aria-label="Resolution steps">
            {steps.map((step, index) => <li data-step-item={index} data-state={index === 0 ? 'current' : 'upcoming'}>
              <h4 class="augur-type-heading-2">
                <span class="static-step"><span class="step-number">0{index + 1}</span>{step.title}</span>
                <button type="button" data-resolution-step={index} aria-pressed={index === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'} aria-controls="resolution-visual" hidden>
                  <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">0{index + 1}</span>{step.title}<span class="step-arrow"><Icon name="arrow-right" /></span>
                </button>
              </h4>
              <p class="web-body-small">{step.text}</p>
            </li>)}
          </ol>
          <details class="technical-note process-detail">
            <summary>Timing, fees &amp; Invalid <Icon name="plus" /></summary>
            <div class="technical-body">
              <p>Reporting and appeals have separate time windows. A completed challenge starts a new appeal period; the preview compresses these periods and makes no timing promise.</p>
              <p>The January design resolves a query as Invalid if no report arrives within its three-day reporting window. Invalid also covers malformed or unresolvable questions.</p>
              <p>Fees are dynamic. The 15 REP example comes from §4.5. A portion pays the first reporter of the final outcome; the remainder is burned.</p>
              <p class="section-reference">January 2026 whitepaper · §§4.1, 4.3–4.5</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>

        <div>
          <figure class="resolution-visual" id="resolution-visual" aria-label="Example of an Augur Lituus query">
            <div class="query-toolbar">
              <span class="query-identity augur-type-control">Example query</span>
              <span class="query-status" data-query-status role="status">Open</span>
            </div>
            <div class="query-body">
              <p class="example-question augur-type-heading-2">Will room-temperature superconductivity at ambient pressure be independently demonstrated?</p>
              <details class="query-criteria technical-note" data-query-criteria>
                <summary>Question criteria <Icon name="plus" /></summary>
                <div class="technical-body">
                  <dl>
                    <div><dt>Required result</dt><dd>Zero electrical resistance within disclosed uncertainty and magnetic-field expulsion (the Meissner effect), at 20°C or above and 90–110 kPa absolute pressure.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Independent replication</dt><dd>An original experiment and replication at a separate institution, with no shared authors and independently prepared samples.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Evidence cutoff · 8 Sep 2027, 00:00 UTC</dt><dd>Both teams must publish methods, measurements and uncertainty in papers or public preprints strictly before the cutoff. Announcements or levitation videos alone do not qualify.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Outcomes</dt><dd>Yes if every requirement is met; otherwise No, including missing replication. Invalid if the question is malformed or unresolvable.</dd></div>
                  </dl>
                </div>
              </details>
              <p class="example-evidence">Example scenario: no qualifying replication by the deadline.</p>
              <div class="visual-scenes">
                {scenes.map((scene, index) => <div class="visual-scene" data-resolution-scene={index} data-active={index === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'} aria-hidden={index !== 0 ? 'true' : undefined} inert={index !== 0}>
                  <span class="field-label" data-scene-label>{scene.label}</span>
                  <strong class:list={['scene-answer', { 'scene-outcomes': index === 0 }]} data-scene-answer>{scene.answer}</strong>
                  <p class="scene-note" data-scene-note>{scene.note}</p>
                  <div class="bond-receipt"><span data-scene-cost>{scene.cost}</span><strong><span data-scene-amount>{scene.amount}</span> <span class="rep-unit">REP</span></strong></div>
                </div>)}
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="query-controls" data-step-controls hidden>
              <button type="button" class:list={[buttonVariants({ variant: 'outline' }), 'configured-button']} data-resolution-previous aria-label="Previous step" disabled><Icon name="arrow-right" /></button>
              <span class="step-counter" data-step-count>01 / 04</span>
              <button type="button" class:list={[buttonVariants(), 'configured-button']} data-resolution-next>Next step</button>
            </div>
            <div class="query-progress" aria-hidden="true">{steps.map((_, index) => <span data-query-progress={index}></span>)}</div>
          </figure>
          <div class="example-options" data-example-options hidden>
            <span data-path-label>Without a challenge</span>
            <button type="button" data-challenge-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="resolution-visual"><span data-challenge-label>See a challenge</span><Icon name="plus" /></button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="source-line">
      <a href={whitepaperUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">January 2026 whitepaper <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</HomeSection>

<script>
  import { initResolutionExplainer } from '../../motion/resolution-explainer';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-why-how]').forEach(initResolutionExplainer);
</script>

<style>
  /* The section heading and lead come from HomeSection. Three cells in one outlined strip, with a 5px
     square on every line crossing: the hero's squares (3px texture) grown into junctions. The list's background shows through its padding and gaps as the lines, so the strip
     reveals as one piece. Subgrid rows keep the marks, titles and text level across the cells. */
  .principles {
    position: relative; isolation: isolate; list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 1px;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0 1px; background: var(--web-outline);
  }
  .principles li { position: relative; display: grid; grid-row: span 2; grid-template-rows: subgrid; row-gap: 0; min-width: 0; padding: 20px; background: var(--background); }
  /* Each cell marks the two crossings on its left edge; the list marks the two on the far right. */
  .principles::before, .principles::after, .principles li::before, .principles li::after {
    content: ''; position: absolute; z-index: 1; width: 5px; height: 5px; background: var(--muted-foreground);
  }
  .principles li::before { top: -3px; left: -3px; }
  .principles li::after { bottom: -3px; left: -3px; }
  .principles::before { top: -2px; right: -2px; }
  .principles::after { bottom: -2px; right: -2px; }
  .principles h3 { font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.3; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .principles p { margin-top: 8px; color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .process-story { margin-top: 96px; }
  /* A subsection heading: below the section's 50px heading, above the card titles. */
  .process-heading { display: grid; gap: 14px; margin: 0 0 40px; }
  .process-heading h3 { font-size: 36px; line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -.03em; }
  .process-heading > p { color: var(--muted-foreground); font-size: 13px; }
  .process-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .9fr 1.1fr; gap: 64px; align-items: start; }
  .process-steps { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .process-steps li { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-quiet); padding-block: 16px; }
  .process-steps li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-quiet); }
  .process-steps h4 { margin: 0; font-size: 18px; line-height: 26px; }
  .static-step, .process-steps button { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; }
  .process-steps button { width: 100%; padding: 0; color: inherit; border: 0; background: none; text-align: left; font: inherit; cursor: pointer; }
  [data-enhanced] .static-step { display: none; }
  .step-number { display: grid; place-items: center; flex-shrink: 0; width: 28px; height: 28px; border: 1px solid var(--border-quiet); font: 400 11px/1 var(--augur-font-secondary); color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .step-arrow { visibility: hidden; margin-left: auto; }
  .step-arrow :global(.web-icon) { width: 17px; height: 17px; }
  [data-enhanced] [data-state="current"] .step-number { background: var(--primary); border-color: var(--primary); color: var(--primary-foreground); }
  [data-enhanced] [data-state="current"] .step-arrow { visibility: visible; }
  .process-steps button:hover .step-number { border-color: var(--foreground); }
  .process-steps li > p { margin: 8px 0 0 42px; max-width: 45ch; color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .technical-note > summary { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; min-height: 44px; cursor: pointer; list-style: none; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .technical-note > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .technical-note > summary:hover, .technical-note[open] > summary { color: var(--foreground); }
  .technical-note > summary :global(.web-icon) { width: 14px; height: 14px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .technical-note[open] > summary :global(.web-icon) { transform: rotate(45deg); }
  .technical-body { padding-block: 8px 16px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .technical-body p + p { margin-top: 12px; }
  .technical-body .section-reference { font-size: 11px; }
  .technical-body dl { margin: 0; }
  .technical-body dl > div + div { margin-top: 14px; }
  .technical-body dt { color: var(--foreground); font-weight: 600; }
  .technical-body dd { margin: 4px 0 0; }
  .process-detail { margin-left: 42px; }
  .resolution-visual { position: relative; border: 1px solid var(--web-outline); background: var(--background); }
  .query-toolbar { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 16px; padding: 16px 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-quiet); }
  .query-identity { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .query-status { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; padding: 5px 10px; font-size: 11px; white-space: nowrap; border: 1px solid var(--border-quiet); background: var(--muted); }
  .query-status::before { content: ''; width: 5px; height: 5px; background: currentColor; }
  [data-current-step="3"] .query-status { color: var(--primary-foreground); border-color: var(--primary); background: var(--primary); }
  .query-body { padding: 22px 24px 18px; }
  .example-question { font-size: clamp(19px, 1.6vw, 24px); line-height: 1.4; letter-spacing: -.025em; max-width: 40ch; }
  .query-criteria > summary { justify-content: start; width: fit-content; gap: 10px; }
  .query-criteria .technical-body { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-quiet); }
  .example-evidence { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted-foreground); padding-top: 4px; }
  .visual-scenes { display: grid; margin-top: 18px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-quiet); }
  .visual-scene { grid-area: 1 / 1; display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-width: 0; }
  .visual-scene:not([data-active="true"]) { visibility: hidden; pointer-events: none; }
  .field-label { color: var(--muted-foreground); font-size: 11px; }
  .scene-answer { display: block; margin-top: 6px; font: 600 38px/1.2 var(--augur-font-primary); letter-spacing: -.03em; }
  .scene-outcomes { font-size: 21px; line-height: 45.6px; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .scene-note { margin-top: 10px; min-height: 42px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted-foreground); max-width: 48ch; }
  .bond-receipt { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 16px; margin-top: auto; padding-top: 20px; }
  .bond-receipt > span { font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .bond-receipt > strong { font: 600 21px/1.3 var(--augur-font-primary); }
  .rep-unit { font: 400 11px/1.3 var(--augur-font-secondary); color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .query-controls { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; padding: 0 24px 22px; }
  .query-controls button:first-child { padding-inline: 15px; }
  .query-controls button:first-child :global(.web-icon) { transform: rotate(180deg); }
  .query-controls :global(.web-icon) { width: 16px; height: 16px; }
  .query-controls button:disabled { opacity: .4; }
  .step-counter { font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted-foreground); margin-right: auto; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .query-progress { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 3px; }
  .query-progress > span { height: 3px; background: var(--border-quiet); }
  .query-progress > span[data-complete] { background: var(--primary); }
  .example-options { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; padding-top: 10px; min-height: 44px; font-size: 12px; }
  .example-options > span { color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .example-options button { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; min-height: 40px; padding: 0; border: 0; background: transparent; color: var(--foreground); font: inherit; cursor: pointer; }
  .example-options :global(.web-icon) { width: 14px; height: 14px; }
  .example-options button[aria-pressed="true"] :global(.web-icon) { transform: rotate(45deg); }
  .source-line { display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; padding-top: 24px; margin-top: 32px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-quiet); font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.65; }
  .source-line a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; color: var(--foreground); text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap; }
  .source-line a:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .source-line :global(.web-icon) { width: 14px; height: 14px; }
  button:focus-visible, summary:focus-visible, a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--foreground); outline-offset: 4px; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) { .step-number { transition: color 180ms ease, background-color 180ms ease; } }
  @media (max-width: 1100px) {
    .process-layout { gap: 32px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .process-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; }
    .principles { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1px; }
    .principles li { display: flex; flex-direction: column; grid-row: auto; }
  }
</style>
